From 45b8d4bc8690d064c315cbf026c189e58f3e0b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: weldensieteklay <weldensieteklay@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 04:29:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add downloadable User Guide (PDF) with "User Guide" button on
 each screen

Add a "User Guide" button next to the existing "Guide Me" button on the
Dashboard, Cross-Sectional, Time Series, and Panel Data screens. Clicking it
downloads a formatted PDF user guide (served as a static asset from
frontend/public/user-guide.pdf).

- New reusable UserGuideButton component (anchor download link with icon)
- Wire the button into Dashboard, CrossSectionalData, PanelData, TimeSeriesData
- Add the generated user-guide.pdf to frontend/public so Vite serves/bundles it
- Include the guide source documents (USER_GUIDE.md and USER_GUIDE.docx) at the
  repo root

The guide covers application overview, per-screen step-by-step procedures, data
preparation, worked research examples, result interpretation, troubleshooting,
best practices, and an appendix with the equation form of every model.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011wJbX1tkPFCh6v16uEb34z
